==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|theophania}}, corresponding to {{confix|theo|phany}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/θiːˈɒfəni/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|theophanies}}

# A manifestation of a [[deity]] to a man.
#* '''2009''', {{w|Karen Armstrong}}, ''The Case for God'', Vintage 2010, p. 47:
#*: It was a bewildering '''theophany''', since it was impossible to make out anything clearly in the stormy obscurity of thunder, lightning, smoke and wind.

